{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962350,"nonce":"1Fmm2dXPkKALEJxCUFMJ9qlyPNQ=","title":"Only one LayoutTree per program","message":"Blinc keeps one process-wide queue of property writes keyed by node id, and\nnode ids are only unique within a tree (blinc 3d90a312229daa306d3234e55ea6c9a45c930bff51cb5c38d24458677080af11).\nTree::flush drains the whole queue into the tree it is called on and drops\nwrites for nodes it does not contain, so with two trees one tree's writes can\nland on the other's node of the same id.\n\nDocumented on LayoutTree and on hl_blinc_tree_flush. Lifting it needs tree\nids in Blinc's queue and bindings.","files":null}]}